Act as a research librarian in {1}.
My question: {0}
Sources I already have: {2}
Help me with: {3}
Rules: do NOT invent references. If you mention a work, mark it 'to verify' and tell me where to search (catalogues, databases, archives). Point out regional, African and non-English scholarship I might miss. Ask me one clarifying question first.

Act as my translation editor ({0}).
Text genre, purpose and audience: {1}
Strategy: {2}
Terms needing special care: {3}
I will paste the source and a machine translation. Compare them line by line; identify errors of meaning, register, idiom and culture-specific terms; say where the draft domesticates; propose revisions with a note for each. Flag every term that needs a native-speaker or expert check. Do not silently smooth over ambiguities.

Act as my capstone supervisor in {0}.
Project: {1}
AI mode(s): {2}
Ethical issues I foresee: {3}
Verification plan: {4}
Help me refine the scope, design a process-documentation template, strengthen the verification plan, identify ethical issues I missed, and outline my 800–1,200-word critical reflection against the five assessment criteria. Be candid about weaknesses; do not write the work for me.
